"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTg="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":true,"topics":["hacktoberfest"],"visibility":"public","forks":3764,"open_issues":978,"watchers":4355,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Maintainer: @stangri\r\nEnvironment: aarch64, r16357-f8669c174e (Raspberry Pi 4 snapshot as of 2021-03-29)\r\n\r\nDescription:\r\n\r\nThere is a persistent and gradual memory leak in https-dns-proxy, at least using default settings:\r\n\r\n```\r\nconfig main 'config'\r\n        option update_dnsmasq_config '*'\r\n        list force_dns_port '53'\r\n        list force_dns_port '853'\r\n        option force_dns '1'\r\n\r\nconfig https-dns-proxy\r\n        option listen_addr '127.0.0.1'\r\n        option user 'nobody'\r\n        option group 'nogroup'\r\n        option listen_port '5053'\r\n        option bootstrap_dns '8.8.8.8,8.8.4.4'\r\n        option resolver_url 'https://dns.google/dns-query'\r\n\r\nconfig https-dns-proxy\r\n        option bootstrap_dns '1.1.1.1,1.0.0.1,2606:4700:4700::1111,2606:4700:4700::1001'\r\n        option resolver_url 'https://cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query'\r\n        option listen_port '5054'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis can be pretty clearly demonstrated with a memory profile:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7516483/116002018-957bf000-a5c5-11eb-9db9-4f1e0d274627.png)\r\n\r\nUsage patterns are typical of a 5-person household (2 working from home, 2 high school age children in remote learning) with standard usage patterns (video streaming, web browsing, Zoom sessions, etc.).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/packages/issues/15513/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/packages/issues/15513/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event